\
## What the Project is Doing\
\
The project is producing a coherent, sequential evidence base that moves from policy diagnosis to implementation roadmap. Nine deliverables (D1\'96D9) cover legal and regulatory analysis, cost and economic viability, local manufacturing and skills, electrification and grid constraints, policy briefs, a national advocacy framework, a comprehensive synthesis report, a stakeholder validation engagement, and a public awareness mini-documentary.\
\
Methodologically, the project combines comprehensive policy review, primary survey data collection through KoboToolbox across nine districts, Total Cost of Ownership (TCO) modelling, GIS-based infrastructure mapping, Bayesian Ridge Regression analysis of registration and tariff data, and structured skills assessment workshops. Gender Equality and Social Inclusion (GESI) is mainstreamed throughout, guided by a dedicated Gender Advisory Committee inaugurated at project launch.\
\
