## Stakeholders and Partners\
\
The project draws together government, regulators, private-sector e-mobility operators, civil society, and development partners. Engagement has included the Ministry of Transport, Ministry of Energy and Green Transition, Ministry of State for Climate Change and Sustainability, Energy Commission, Driver and Vehicle Licensing Authority (DVLA), Ghana Standards Authority, Environmental Protection Agency, Public Utilities Regulatory Commission, ECG, NEDCo and GRIDCo. Private-sector partners include SolarTaxi Ghana, Wahu Mobility, Apsonic, Charge Express, and SmartWatt. NorvanReports serves as the project's communications partner, and the GAC anchors civil-society representation. Development partner engagement spans UNDP, GIZ, World Bank, and AfDB.\
\
*[Suggested image: Inception meeting / stakeholder workshop photo]*\
\
